+## Custom store path
+
+By default tally reads and writes `tally.json` in the current directory. Use
+`--store` to point it somewhere else:
+
+```bash
+python -m tally.cli --store ~/finances/2024.json add 50 rent
+```
+
+This makes it easy to keep separate files for separate years or purposes.
+
